<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- CHIMERA shim runs as root via LaunchDaemon and needs NO special entitlements:
         it opens one local socket, execs nothing operator-provided, reads no files (§8.8).
         Hardened runtime (codesign --options runtime) is applied with an empty entitlement
         set — the strictest posture.

         Module capabilities that look like they might need entitlements do NOT:
           - MIRROR CGEventTap  -> Accessibility is a TCC GRANT (System Settings), not an entitlement
           - TETHER CoreBluetooth -> Bluetooth is a TCC GRANT + an Info.plist usage string
         Add real entitlements here only if a future signed binary genuinely requires one,
         and only alongside the matching §8 review. -->
</dict>
</plist>
